# Hakum · Archify in the principal workflow

This repo already mandates **graphify** before code exploration. **Archify** is the diagram layer for the same principal full-stack bar.

## Triggers (read `archify` skill and deliver HTML)

Use Archify (validate → deliver → visual-check) when documenting or designing:

- Money triangle: POS → End of shift → Finance accept → floor payroll
- Queue `QUEUE_STATUS_TRANSITIONS` / wash–detail lifecycle
- Booking → attendance → TL → BA → SA role paths (shop-day FLOPS)
- Finance kind / drawer / payroll contract dataflow
- Supabase RPC sequences for shift-close reopen / payroll confirm
- Any Mermaid in `docs/` that should become a showcase artifact

## Conventions

- Spec + HTML live under `docs/architecture/` (create if missing)
- Name files by concern: e.g. `money-path.workflow.json` + `money-path.workflow.html`
- Prefer `workflow`, `sequence`, `lifecycle`, `dataflow`, or `architecture` types from the Archify skill
- Ground nodes in graphify evidence (`graphify query "…"`) — do not invent RPCs or pages
- After code changes that alter those paths: `graphify update .`; refresh Archify only when the diagram claim changed

## Finish bar

Do not call architecture docs “done” without Archify `deliver` exit 0 (and note visual-check status honestly). Production ops blockers (customer reminder BrandTxt IP / Auth SMTP) stay documented separately — never diagram them as closed without host proof. **No owner daily SMS** — outbound customer reminders only; Finance accept uses web push.

## SMS policy (always)

- BusyBee: outbound customer status/reminders only · **no inbound replies**
- **No owner daily close SMS** (legacy `ENABLE_OWNER_SMS=1` QA-only)
- Never treat owner handset env as a readiness gate

## CLI (global skill install)

```bash
node "$HOME/.agents/skills/archify/bin/archify.mjs" doctor
node "$HOME/.agents/skills/archify/bin/archify.mjs" validate <type> <spec.json> --quality showcase --json
node "$HOME/.agents/skills/archify/bin/archify.mjs" deliver <type> <spec.json> <out.html> --quality showcase --json
```

On Windows PowerShell, use `$env:USERPROFILE\.agents\skills\archify\bin\archify.mjs`.

